Flemming Kraglund from RC International, Copenhagen, Denmark writes:

>I made a suggestion like that one or perhaps two years ago, and I really
>like the idea. Basically use XRD (external data representaion) for the
>bone files and text for the score files. Destribute via News (r.g.h.data?)
>Only send new top scores (or perhaps amoung the top ten) from a site, so as
>not to clobber the net with those quick deaths.


This is a very intriguing idea.  There would never be a lack of bones files
for players on PCs or small machines.  They could be manually offloaded
from news, or a cron job could extract them into the playground
automatically.  NetHack would even more live up to its name, as a sort
of shared dungeon by the players on UseNet.  Eventually, level files
could be handled the same way.

